# SwiftFormat configuration for MacConnect.
#
# Bonus-2 baseline. The codebase's existing style is the target — these
# settings track what's already in tree so swiftformat --lint can run in
# CI without rewriting everything.

--indent 4
--swiftversion 5.9
--tabwidth 4
--maxwidth 120
--wraparguments preserve
--wrapparameters preserve
--wrapcollections preserve
--commas inline
--trimwhitespace always
--ifdef no-indent
# `--self` defaults to `remove`, which strips `self.` inside os.Logger
# string interpolation. The compiler rejects that because Logger's
# interpolation arguments are @autoclosure @escaping. SwiftFormat does
# not reason about that rule, so we disable `redundantSelf` entirely
# and let the codebase use `self.` wherever it currently does.
--disable redundantSelf
--patternlet inline
--linebreaks lf
--semicolons never
--header strip
--exclude .build,build
